//
// windows-1252, ISO-8859-15 and macintosh come from the WHATWG Encoding
// Standard's indexes (what browsers decode); IBM 437, IBM 850, IBM 037 and
// IBM 500 from the Unicode Consortium's archived vendor mapping tables, which
// the Consortium keeps "only for historical and archival purposes" and
// without a guarantee that they match any platform. Every table was compared
// byte for byte with CPython 3.11's codecs and glibc 2.39's iconv on
// 2026-10-03: the only differences are windows-1252's 0x81, 0x8D, 0x8F, 0x90
// and 0x9D (WHATWG maps them to the C1 controls U+0081 to U+009D; CPython and
// iconv leave them undefined) and two bytes of macintosh in iconv (0xC6 as
// U+0394 instead of U+2206, 0xF0 as U+E01E instead of U+F8FF).
//
// ASCII-compatible tables store only bytes 0x80-0xFF (bytes 0x00-0x7F map to
// themselves in all of them); the two EBCDIC tables store all 256 bytes.
// Every value is in the Basic Multilingual Plane and every table is
// one-to-one, so encoding is the exact inverse of decoding.
// ============================================================================

